WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.929
The omnichannel reports show how your team's calls, texts and follow-ups are going,

00:00:05.929 --> 00:00:07.978
from first lead to closed deal.

00:00:07.978 --> 00:00:12.740
This video shows which report answers which question, and how the Report Builder

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.180
reads the same data.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.172
Every call, text and follow-up is an activity.

00:00:22.172 --> 00:00:26.803
A personal list cannot show how much work is open, who is behind,

00:00:26.803 --> 00:00:28.760
or which campaign works.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:37.353
The omnichannel reports answer those questions from your activities, campaigns, dispositions, leads and opportunities.

00:00:37.353 --> 00:00:42.730
These slides only introduce the ideas; every report is shown on the real pages.

00:00:46.932 --> 00:00:49.494
Open Reports in the admin menu.

00:00:49.494 --> 00:00:56.002
The omnichannel reports sit in several categories, most of them under CRM and Campaigns.

00:00:56.453 --> 00:00:58.378
Open Activity summary.

00:00:58.378 --> 00:01:06.834
The activity reports share the filters Date range, Campaign group, Campaign, Channel, Source, Status and Disposition.

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:10.133
Show runs the report, and Export saves it.

00:01:11.735 --> 00:01:18.736
Each report needs the View Omnichannel reports permission, set per role under Access Control, Roles.

00:01:18.736 --> 00:01:22.435
Administrators and Supervisors have it by default.

00:01:26.636 --> 00:01:29.638
Activity summary is the daily view:

00:01:29.638 --> 00:01:35.569
total, completed with its rate, pending, in progress, failed and cancelled.

00:01:35.569 --> 00:01:39.376
Bars split them by source, channel and status.

00:01:39.826 --> 00:01:45.706
Campaign performance has one row per campaign, and a second table per campaign group.

00:01:46.156 --> 00:01:53.616
Disposition breakdown counts completed activities by the disposition chosen, and its share of all completions.

00:01:57.802 --> 00:02:01.145
Activity backlog looks at all work still open.

00:02:01.145 --> 00:02:06.416
Unassigned has no owner, Overdue is past its scheduled time, and Reserved is

00:02:06.416 --> 00:02:08.602
held for an agent right now.

00:02:09.053 --> 00:02:13.956
Activity aging puts the same work into age bands, from under an hour

00:02:13.956 --> 00:02:15.613
to over seven days.

00:02:15.613 --> 00:02:18.993
A heavy last band is old work nobody touches.

00:02:19.443 --> 00:02:24.156
Overdue workload by user shows who holds the late work, how much is

00:02:24.156 --> 00:02:27.383
unassigned, and its average and maximum age.

00:02:31.564 --> 00:02:35.741
Several reports share one table and change the grouping.

00:02:35.741 --> 00:02:39.178
Activity source performance groups by origin:

00:02:39.178 --> 00:02:45.107
manual, automatic by AI, callback, or a dialer mode, with the outcomes, completion

00:02:45.107 --> 00:02:47.264
rate and average attempts.

00:02:47.716 --> 00:02:53.764
CRM channel performance groups by Phone or SMS, Activity kind performance by call

00:02:53.764 --> 00:02:57.936
or text, and Contact type workload by Lead or Contact.

00:02:58.394 --> 00:03:04.900
Activity assignment performance groups by assignment status, and Activity urgency performance by urgency,

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:07.654
to check that urgent work finishes first.

00:03:08.105 --> 00:03:14.428
Activity attempt analysis shows how many attempts each activity needed and how many completed.

00:03:14.428 --> 00:03:20.055
Scheduled completion performance compares work finished on schedule with late work.

00:03:24.245 --> 00:03:30.658
Assigned user performance gives each person's activities, outcomes and completion rate.

00:03:30.658 --> 00:03:33.555
Work nobody owns appears as Not set.

00:03:34.006 --> 00:03:39.616
User completion time shows the average, median and maximum time finished work took.

00:03:39.616 --> 00:03:43.966
Daily user productivity gives the same for each person and day.

00:03:44.417 --> 00:03:49.922
Activity creation by user shows who or what created the work, for audits.

00:03:49.922 --> 00:03:53.197
Not set is work with no recorded creator.

00:03:57.385 --> 00:04:02.833
Four campaign reports break each campaign down by source, channel, disposition and number

00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:06.045
of attempts, with the completion rate of each row.

00:04:06.496 --> 00:04:12.256
Customer workload has one row per customer, to spot someone contacted too often.

00:04:12.707 --> 00:04:17.747
Address usage compares your sales line, support line and text line.

00:04:21.942 --> 00:04:27.516
Dialer call detail lists one row per number the dialer worked, with contact,

00:04:27.516 --> 00:04:31.662
campaign, last disposition, attempts, agent and status.

00:04:31.662 --> 00:04:35.332
It opens on the Dialer source, a page at a time.

00:04:35.788 --> 00:04:41.248
AI handoff and containment counts the conversations an AI profile finished itself and

00:04:41.248 --> 00:04:45.208
those it passed to a live agent, with the rates, the time to

00:04:45.208 --> 00:04:47.068
escalate and the reasons.

00:04:51.341 --> 00:04:57.599
Lead funnel shows leads created in the period by their current status, and the conversion rate.

00:04:57.599 --> 00:05:00.821
The three CRM reports use the date range only.

00:05:01.298 --> 00:05:06.693
Lead conversion by source and list shows, for each, how many leads converted,

00:05:06.693 --> 00:05:09.748
the rate and the average time to convert.

00:05:10.271 --> 00:05:15.662
Opportunity pipeline lists open deals by stage with amount and weighted amount, using

00:05:15.662 --> 00:05:21.291
the stage's probability, then the win rate and amount won for deals closed in the period.

00:05:25.472 --> 00:05:28.685
The Report Builder reads the same records.

00:05:28.685 --> 00:05:33.102
Open Reports, Report Builder, New Report, then Add data set.

00:05:34.451 --> 00:05:41.689
The Omnichannel source offers Activities, Dispositions, Campaigns, Campaign groups and Activity batches.

00:05:41.689 --> 00:05:45.901
Contacts, leads and opportunities are under Content items.

00:05:46.364 --> 00:05:47.598
Add Activities.

00:05:47.598 --> 00:05:52.594
The window then lists related data sets, such as the activity's disposition and

00:05:52.594 --> 00:05:55.004
campaign, which are joined for you.

00:05:55.454 --> 00:06:02.314
The Messaging source offers Conversations and Messages, with each outbound text's delivery status

00:06:02.314 --> 00:06:03.979
but never its text.

00:06:03.979 --> 00:06:05.244
Add Messages.

00:06:05.694 --> 00:06:10.643
Drag Delivery status and Number of rows onto Columns, and the preview counts

00:06:10.643 --> 00:06:12.514
texts by delivery status.

00:06:16.701 --> 00:06:18.240
Morning stand-up:

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:24.396
a supervisor opens Activity backlog, then Overdue workload by user, and reassigns late

00:06:24.396 --> 00:06:26.471
work before anyone dials.

00:06:26.928 --> 00:06:28.283
Campaign review:

00:06:28.283 --> 00:06:35.428
compare Campaign performance, Campaign disposition mix and Lead conversion to decide which campaign to repeat.

00:06:35.878 --> 00:06:37.025
AI rollout:

00:06:37.025 --> 00:06:39.654
watch AI handoff and containment.

00:06:39.654 --> 00:06:45.251
A falling containment rate, or a common escalation reason, shows where the AI

00:06:45.251 --> 00:06:47.948
profile needs better instructions.

00:06:49.948 --> 00:06:56.244
The omnichannel reports turn activities, campaigns, leads and deals into numbers you can act on.

00:06:56.244 --> 00:06:57.848
Thanks for watching.

